seq v=1 rig=screen program=claude build=2.1.0
# §2.4: a box the person stops the turn under (Esc, or the box's own "No")
# closes `declined`. The screen reports the interrupt (Claude Code's
# `⎿  Interrupted · What should Claude do instead?` under the call the box
# asked about) with the idle it publishes next, and that verdict closes the
# box; the person's key bound to the box makes the close theirs, as any other.
# The report holds for that one verdict: a box a later verdict closes passed.
see busy
half
see prompt bash:not-read-only fixture=claude-2.1.280-box-bash-touch
expect open p1 approval par=t1 box=bash:not-read-only @500
person
at 700 interrupted
see idle fixture=claude-2.1.316-box-bash-declined-esc
expect close p1 approval out=declined by=human @700
half
half
expect close t1 turn out=interrupted
at 3000 see busy
at 3200 interrupted
see prompt bash:not-read-only
expect open p2 approval par=t2 box=bash:not-read-only @3200
at 3400 see busy
expect close p2 approval out=passed @3400
